<div class="page-header">
  <div>
    <h1 class="page-title">Paystack Configuration</h1>
    <p class="page-subtitle">Quick check that your Paystack API keys are loaded correctly.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="admin-card">
  <h2 class="admin-card-title">Status</h2>

  <table class="admin-table">
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 220px;">Configured</th>
        <td>
          <% if (result.configured) { %>
            <span class="badge badge-success">Yes</span>
          <% } else { %>
            <span class="badge badge-warning">No (using mock checkout)</span>
          <% } %>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Public key set</th>
        <td>
          <% if (result.publicKeySet) { %>
            <span class="badge badge-success">Yes</span>
          <% } else { %>
            <span class="badge badge-muted">No</span>
          <% } %>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Secret key set</th>
        <td>
          <% if (result.secretKeySet) { %>
            <span class="badge badge-success">Yes</span>
            <span style="font-size: 12px; color: #6c757d; margin-left: 8px;">(prefix: <code><%= result.secretKeyPrefix %></code>)</span>
          <% } else { %>
            <span class="badge badge-muted">No</span>
          <% } %>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p class="text-muted" style="margin: 18px 0 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6;">
    To configure Paystack, set <code>PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY</code> and <code>PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY</code> in your <code>.env</code> file.
    Use <code>pk_test_</code> / <code>sk_test_</code> prefixes for testing and <code>pk_live_</code> / <code>sk_live_</code> for production.
    Restart the server after changing <code>.env</code>.
  </p>

  <p class="text-muted" style="margin: 10px 0 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6;">
    When Paystack is not configured, applications use a mock checkout page that simulates a successful payment
    so you can test the full flow without real charges.
  </p>
</div>